":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"closed\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":2,\"created_at\":\"2023-11-13T18:23:35Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2024-03-25T19:49:51Z\",\"closed_at\":\"2023-11-14T05:06:10Z\",\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"draft\":false,\"pull_request\":{\"url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/pulls/50\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/hypertidy/ncmeta/pull/50\",\"diff_url\":\"https://github.com/hypertidy/ncmeta/pull/50.diff\",\"patch_url\":\"https://github.com/hypertidy/ncmeta/pull/50.patch\",\"merged_at\":\"2023-11-14T05:06:10Z\"},\"body\":\"This PR is for attaching extended attributes to the ncmeta() output. Currently, any \\\"time\\\" dimension that conforms to the CF Metadata Conventions will be interpreted with the CFtime package. Other extended attributes can be integrated easily.\",\"closed_by\":{\"login\":\"mdsumner\",\"id\":4107631,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMDc2MzE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4107631?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/mdsumner\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/50/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/50/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null},{\"url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/49\",\"repository_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta\",\"labels_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/49/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/49/comments\",\"events_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/49/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/49\",\"id\":1967060013,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOBZkC0M51PvQt\",\"number\":49,\"title\":\"Extended metadata for \\\"time\\\" dimension and possible others\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"pvanlaake\",\"id\":8315731,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgzMTU3MzE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8315731?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/pvanlaake\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"closed\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":8,\"created_at\":\"2023-10-29T16:33:42Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2024-03-26T08:57:09Z\",\"closed_at\":\"2024-03-26T08:57:08Z\",\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"NetCDF has a very well-defined structure for describing data that goes into the file, `ncmeta` already captures all this information nicely. There are several conventions based on the basic NetCDF structure for additional standards, with COARDS and the CF Metadata Conventions among the more popular ones. I would assume that >90% of NetCDF data that is publicly exchanged (meaning, where the data consumer is not familiar with the processing design of the data producer and thus dependent on the metadata and any conventions to interpret the data) follows one of these conventions. To me it would therefore make sense to try and capture some of these conventions to describe domain-specific concepts into `ncmeta` and thus make them more accessible to NetCDF consumers in R.\\r\\n\\r\\nI would propose to call these \\\"extended metadata\\\" and to capture them in an additional `tibble` called (let me think hard here) `extended` that is attached to the result of passing a NetCDF resource through this package. For the \\\"time\\\" dimension used by both COARDS and the CF Metadata Conventions, notoriously hard to interpret due to its in-built flexibility, that would look somewhat like this:\\r\\n\\r\\n```r\\r\\nnc_meta.NetCDF <- function(x, ...) {\\r\\n  (...)\\r\\n  \\r\\n  atts <- nc_atts(x) ## safe to assume there are always some attributes - it's the raison d'etre of NetCDF\\r\\n  \\r\\n  ## Add time information for any \\\"time\\\" dimension. Since not all files have a \\r\\n  ## \\\"calendar\\\" attribute or \\\"axis == \\\"T\\\"\\\", just try to create a CFtime\\r\\n  ## instance for any dimension variable with a \\\"units\\\" attribute and a \\r\\n  ## \\\"calendar\\\", if present. Build a tibble for extended metadata from \\r\\n  ## identified time dimensions.\\r\\n  idx <- which(atts$name == \\\"units\\\")\\r\\n  var_names <- atts$variable[idx]\\r\\n  units <- unlist(atts$value[idx])\\r\\n  ext <- tibble::tibble()\\r\\n  for (i in seq_along(idx)) {\\r\\n    if (nchar(units)[i] < 8) next\\r\\n    cal <- unlist(atts$value[which(atts$variable == var_names[i] & atts$name == \\\"calendar\\\")])\\r\\n    try({\\r\\n      cft <- CFtime::CFtime(units[i], cal)\\r\\n      ## we have a CFtime instance so now read actual offsets and add\\r\\n      offsets <- as.vector(RNetCDF::var.get.nc(x, var_names[i]))\\r\\n      cft <- cft + offsets\\r\\n      \\r\\n      ## add to the tibble\\r\\n      if (nrow(ext) == 0) ext <- tibble::tibble_row(dim_id = dims$id[which(dims$name == var_names[i])], time = cft)\\r\\n      else ext <- tibble::add_row(ext, dim_id = dims$id[which(dims$name == var_names[i])], time = cft)\\r\\n    }, silent = TRUE)\\r\\n  }\\r\\n\\r\\n  structure(list(dimension = dims, \\r\\n       variable = vars, \\r\\n       attribute = atts,\\r\\n       extended = ext,\\r\\n       axis = axis,\\r\\n       grid = nc_grids_dimvar(dims, vars, axis)),\\r\\n       class = \\\"ncmeta\\\")\\r\\n}\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nAlternatively, the extended attributes, like `cft` above, can be added as an additional column to the `dims` tibble.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe `CFtime` package used here can ingest the NetCDF attributes attached to a dimension that represents time and produce a vector of character strings that can be used as `dimnames()`, among several other things. It is currently integrated into the dev version of `tidync` but may actually be better placed here as it then becomes available to all packages that are using `ncmeta`.\\r\\n\\r\\nA similar approach may be used for coordinate reference systems, or other such conventions out there.\",\"closed_by\":{\"login\":\"pvanlaake\",\"id\":8315731,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgzMTU3MzE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8315731?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/pvanlaake\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/49/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/49/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":\"completed\",\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/48\",\"repository_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta\",\"labels_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/48/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/48/comments\",\"events_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/48/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/48\",\"id\":1961802635,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOBZkC0M507ruL\",\"number\":48,\"title\":\"Bounds are not dimensions in CF Metadata Conventions files\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"pvanlaake\",\"id\":8315731,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgzMTU3MzE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8315731?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/pvanlaake\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/pvanlaake/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":8,\"created_at\":\"2023-10-25T16:25:55Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-07-29T06:46:12Z\",\"closed_at\":null,\"assignee\":null,\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"CF Metadata Conventions use NetCDF files with a sophisticated set of conventions to ease interpretation and analysis of the data. One such convention is to include a `bounds` attribute with each dimension when the data represents cells (rather than point observations on a regular grid) to indicate the boundaries of the cell along the dimension. These bounds are included in the file as 3-D arrays for `lon` and `lat` (including the `time` dimension for reasons unknown to me) and a 2-D array for `time`, with an additional first dimension called `bnds`. As per the [CF documentation](http://cfconventions.org/Data/cf-conventions/cf-conventions-1.10/cf-conventions.html#cell-boundaries), \\\"a boundary variable is considered to be part of a coordinate variable’s metadata\\\" and it is thus not a dimension. This is made clear also by the fact that for \\\"dimension\\\" `bnds` `coord_dim == FALSE`. See below example using `tidync`:\\r\\n\\r\\n```r\\r\\n> huss <- tidync(lf[1])\\r\\n> huss\\r\\n\\r\\nData Source (1): huss_day_EC-Earth3-CC_historical_r1i1p1f1_gr_19910101-19960321_v20210113.nc ...\\r\\n\\r\\nGrids (7) <dimension family> : <associated variables> \\r\\n\\r\\n[1]   D1,D2,D0 : lat_bnds    **ACTIVE GRID** ( 976384  values per variable)\\r\\n[2]   D1,D3,D0 : lon_bnds\\r\\n[3]   D3,D2,D0 : huss\\r\\n[4]   D1,D0    : time_bnds\\r\\n[5]   D0       : time\\r\\n[6]   D2       : lat\\r\\n[7]   D3       : lon\\r\\n\\r\\nDimensions 4 (3 active): \\r\\n  \\r\\n  dim   name  length     min     max start count    dmin    dmax unlim coord_dim \\r\\n  <chr> <chr>  <dbl>   <dbl>   <dbl> <int> <int>   <dbl>   <dbl> <lgl> <lgl>     \\r\\n1 D0    time    1907 51500.  53406.      1  1907 51500.  53406.  FALSE TRUE      \\r\\n2 D1    bnds       2     1       2       1     2     1       2   FALSE FALSE     ## <<<<<<<\\r\\n3 D2    lat      256   -89.5    89.5     1   256   -89.5    89.5 FALSE TRUE      \\r\\n  \\r\\nInactive dimensions:\\r\\n  \\r\\n  dim   name  length   min   max unlim coord_dim \\r\\n  <chr> <chr>  <dbl> <dbl> <dbl> <lgl> <lgl>     \\r\\n1 D3    lon      512     0  359. FALSE TRUE  \\r\\n\\r\\n> huss$attribute |> filter(name == \\\"bounds\\\") |> unnest(value)\\r\\n# A tibble: 3 × 4\\r\\n     id name   variable value    \\r\\n  <int> <chr>  <chr>    <chr>    \\r\\n1     0 bounds time     time_bnds\\r\\n2     0 bounds lat      lat_bnds \\r\\n3     0 bounds lon      lon_bnds \\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nWould it be a good idea to drop the `bnds` \\\"dimension\\\" and thus the associated grids? There should be some other mechanism to keep them on, however, such that their contents can be accessed.\\r\\n\",\"closed_by\":null,\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/48/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/48/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":null,\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/47\",\"repository_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta\",\"labels_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/47/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/47/comments\",\"events_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/47/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/47\",\"id\":1477351356,\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOBZkC0M5YDpe8\",\"number\":47,\"title\":\"hyper_tibble\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"lisaholsinger\",\"id\":59367248,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MzY3MjQ4\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59367248?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lisaholsinger\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/lisaholsinger\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lisaholsinger/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lisaholsinger/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lisaholsinger/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lisaholsinger/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lisaholsinger/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lisaholsinger/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lisaholsinger/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lisaholsinger/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/lisaholsinger/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"labels\":[],\"state\":\"closed\",\"locked\":false,\"assignees\":[{\"login\":\"mdsumner\",\"id\":4107631,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMDc2MzE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4107631?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/mdsumner\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false}],\"milestone\":null,\"comments\":10,\"created_at\":\"2022-12-05T20:14:26Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-07-29T02:45:49Z\",\"closed_at\":\"2026-07-29T02:45:48Z\",\"assignee\":{\"login\":\"mdsumner\",\"id\":4107631,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMDc2MzE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4107631?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/mdsumner\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"issue_field_values\":[],\"type\":null,\"active_lock_reason\":null,\"sub_issues_summary\":{\"total\":0,\"completed\":0,\"percent_completed\":0},\"issue_dependencies_summary\":{\"blocked_by\":0,\"total_blocked_by\":0,\"blocking\":0,\"total_blocking\":0},\"body\":\"My apologies for double posting.  I am having issues with hyper_tibble() similar to #42.\\r\\n\\r\\nI am using R 4.2.1, ncmeta 0.3.5, RNetCDF 2.6.1, ncdf4 1.19, tidync 0.3.0 in Windows 10\\r\\n\\r\\nHere is the code below, which previously worked in a R 3.6.2 but now hangs up on the hyper_tibble command.\\r\\nI sure would appreciate any advice! Thank you in advance.\\r\\n\\r\\nlibrary(RNetCDF)\\r\\nlibrary(ncdf4)\\r\\nlibrary(tidync)\\r\\nlibrary(raster)\\r\\nlibrary(tidyverse)\\r\\nlibrary(ncmeta)\\r\\n\\r\\nnc.grid <- tidync('http://thredds.northwestknowledge.net:8080/thredds/dodsC/agg_met_tmmx_1979_CurrentYear_CONUS.nc')\\r\\n\\r\\ngrid.yr <- nc.grid %>% activate(\\\"daily_maximum_temperature\\\") %>%\\r\\nhyper_filter(day = dplyr::between(index, 14784, 14898),\\r\\nlat = dplyr::between(index, 263,319),\\r\\nlon = dplyr::between(index, 387,462))\\r\\n\\r\\ngrid.yr <- grid.yr %>% hyper_tibble()\",\"closed_by\":{\"login\":\"mdsumner\",\"id\":4107631,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMDc2MzE=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4107631?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/mdsumner\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/events{/privacy}\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mdsumner/received_events\",\"type\":\"User\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\",\"site_admin\":false},\"reactions\":{\"url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/47/reactions\",\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0},\"timeline_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/47/timeline\",\"performed_via_github_app\":null,\"state_reason\":\"completed\",\"pinned_comment\":null},{\"url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/46\",\"repository_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta\",\"labels_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/46/labels{/name}\",\"comments_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/46/comments\",\"events_url\":\"ghrepos/hypertidy/ncmeta/issues/46/events\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/hypertidy/ncmeta/pull/46\",\"id\":1460632092,\"node_id\":\"PR_kwDOBZkC0M5DgD7j\",\"number\":46,\"title\":\"#2 - nc_att()/nc_atts()\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"gsapijaszko\",\"id\":20024464,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDI0NDY0\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20024464?v=4\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gsapijaszko\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/gsapijaszko\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gsapijaszko/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gsapijaszko/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gsapijaszko/gists{/gist_id}\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gsapijaszko/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gsapijaszko/subscriptions\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gsapijaszko/orgs\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/gsapijaszko/repos\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.co